{"id":"000W3I","title":"Broken Thermometers","author":"gk122","solvedCount":7,"difficulty":2,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-17T22:57:06+00:00","posted":"Heute, 19:32 Uhr","rules":"I forgot to fasten the thermometers to the grid, and now everything is a mess. Hopefully the puzzle still works out…\n\nRules\n\nNormal 6×6 sudoku rules apply: place the digits 1–6 once each in every row, column and outlined 2×3 box.\n\nBroken thermometers: the thermometers in the grid have been broken into pieces, and each break is shown as a jagged edge.\n\n• A piece with a bulb is the start of a thermometer.\n\n• A piece with a rounded end and no bulb is the end of a thermometer.\n\n• A piece with jagged edges at both ends belongs somewhere in between.\n\nEvery piece is used exactly once: each bulb piece continues through zero or more middle pieces into exactly one end piece. Reading from the bulb through all of its pieces to the end, digits strictly increase, across the breaks too.\n\nWhich pieces belong together, and which way each middle piece runs, must be deduced.\n\nPlay on SudokuPad","solutionCode":"Row 2 of the main puzzle (not the bonus puzzle)","tags":["Sudoku","Thermometer"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/zjm1pvu446","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/zjm1pvu446","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":6,"cols":6,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-17T22:57:06+00:00"}